P0240 CString rejects an exact-fit append by counting two terminators. src/c_string.rs:126. The capacity calculation used by CString::extend_from_bytes counts both the existing trailing nul and the appended slice's trailing nul. Consequently, a CString<5> containing b"ab\0" rejects extend_from_bytes(b"cd\0") with a capacity error, even though the result b"abcd\0" needs exactly five bytes. Callers appending already terminated chunks lose one byte of usable capacity.

